<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="v2-reference"><article><header class="article-top"><div class="article-intro"><a class="article-back" href="<?= e(url('/care-guide')) ?>">← <span>Back to the care notes</span></a><p class="eyebrow">EVERYDAY CARE</p><h1>The art of a gentler finish.</h1><p>You don’t always need another product. A little thought about handling can be part of your care, too.</p><span class="article-meta">AVELA CARE NOTES · 2 MIN READ</span></div><div class="article-visual"><?= handoff_guide_art('finish') ?></div></header><div class="article-body"><nav class="article-outline" aria-label="In this note"><p class="eyebrow">IN THIS NOTE</p><a href="#note-0">Absorb, rather than rub.</a><a href="#note-1">Turn down the heat.</a></nav><div class="article-copy"><section id="note-0"><h2>Absorb, rather than rub.</h2><p>Use a towel or soft T-shirt to absorb water gently. Rubbing hair roughly can add unnecessary friction.</p></section><section id="note-1"><h2>Turn down the heat.</h2><p>Air-dry when you can. If you use heated tools, use a low or medium setting and a suitable heat-protection product as directed. Give your hair breaks from frequent heat styling.</p></section><div class="article-takeaway"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE TAKEAWAY</span><p>Keep handling gentle and follow your product instructions. A routine can be thoughtful without being complicated.</p></div><div class="article-reference">Care reference<br><a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/hair-scalp-care/hair/habits-that-damage-hair" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">American Academy of Dermatology · Hair care habits that can damage hair</a><p>General cosmetic care guidance. Avela does not diagnose or treat hair or scalp conditions.</p></div></div></div></article><section class="guide-cta"><div><h2>Make a little room for you.</h2><p>Bring what you know about your hair into your own routine.</p></div><a class="button primary" href="<?= e(url('/assessment')) ?>">Build my hair profile </a></section></main>
